//@version=5
// Trend-filtered pullback swing, v5 — two modes, one entry.
//
// The entry is unchanged and is the only part of this system that has survived a
// matched-conditions test: RSI(2) below 15 inside a 50/200 uptrend, measured
// against the same exits with no RSI filter, paired on identical dates,
// t = 2.25 over the full history and 2.55 over 2023-2026. Everything else here is
// exit geometry, and exit geometry is where the return actually lives.
//
// TWO MODES. Same signal, opposite temperaments. Measured on 75 large caps,
// 1999-2026, next-open fills, 0.05%/side plus 5 ticks, $50,000 across 20 slots:
//
//                       win    avg win   median hold    $50,000 ->   CAGR   maxDD
//   Conservative       61.6%    +2.35%      12 days       $69,390    1.27%  21.7%
//   Aggressive         33.2%   +25.25%      63 days      $640,803   10.29%  22.5%
//   SPY buy and hold                                     $402,648    8.34%  55.2%
//
// Aggressive is not conservative-with-more-size. It books nothing at the snapback
// and holds to a 12-ATR stop, a break of the 200-day, or 250 bars. You win one
// trade in three. The wins are ten times larger, which is the entire mechanism.
//
// It is a plateau, not a fitted point: all 16 cells of stop/trail 8-15 ATR by
// hold 150-300 bars beat Conservative, best cell $747,996.
//
// WHAT AGGRESSIVE ACTUALLY COSTS YOU:
//   worst single trade      -45.0%   (Conservative -27.1%)
//   worst 1% of trades      -18.5%   (Conservative -10.4%)
//   longest losing streak   40 in a row
//   2022                    -4.63% per trade, $50,000 -> $38,548 in that year
//   2000-2002               -3.09% per trade
// It is NOT uniformly worse in bad markets — it GAINED through 2008-09 (+2.49% per
// trade, $50,000 -> $56,713) because it held survivors into the recovery instead of
// being stopped out repeatedly. It is choppy years, not deep ones, that hurt it.
// One thing it is better at: a run of 10 trades is net negative 30% of the time
// against Conservative's 45%, because the wins are large enough to carry a run.
//
// NOTE: in Aggressive the chandelier trail is INERT. The trail only arms after a
// scale-out, and Aggressive never scales, so its exits are the hard stop, the
// 200-day break, and the bar cap. The trail input is left visible for Custom mode
// but changing it does nothing while scalePercent is 0.
//
// ENTRY-QUALITY FILTERS (rising 200MA / not extended / beats the benchmark) are
// present but default OFF. They looked strong on pooled averages and did not
// survive a paired same-date test: -0.074pp (t=-0.64) on 2022-2026 and +0.052pp
// (t=1.24) on the full history, with the ability to tell a good entry from a bad
// one worth about 0.035pp. What they reliably do is cut exposure (85% deployed to
// 67%), which lowers drawdown by holding less rather than by choosing better. Use
// them as an exposure control if you want one; do not treat them as edge.
//
// ONE SYMBOL IS NOT THE PORTFOLIO. Equal-dollar sizing deploys dollarsPerTrade of
// total equity on the charted symbol, so its return on total equity looks small.
// The figures above come from 75 names competing for 20 slots, which TradingView
// cannot simulate from a single chart. Judge one symbol on expectancy and profit
// factor, not net profit.
//
// STRATEGY TESTER: a scale-out writes TWO closed trades into the trade list, so the
// tester's win rate and expectancy are per exit LEG, not per position. In
// Aggressive there is no scale-out, so its tester figures ARE per position.
//
// NEITHER MODE IS A SAFE SHORT-TERM INCOME STRATEGY. Closing 100% at the snapback
// — the shortest, highest-hit-rate version — turns $50,000 into $44,182 over 26.8
// years. All the return comes from holding a minority of positions far longer than
// is comfortable.
strategy("Trend Pullback Swing v5 [QuantPad]", overlay=true, initial_capital=50000, pyramiding=0, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1, commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05, slippage=5, margin_long=0, margin_short=0, process_orders_on_close=true, calc_on_every_tick=false)

fastLength = input.int(50, "Fast MA length", minval=2, group="Trend filter")
slowLength = input.int(200, "Slow MA length", minval=20, group="Trend filter")

rsiLength = input.int(2, "Pullback RSI length", minval=1, group="Entry")
rsiThreshold = input.int(15, "RSI oversold below", minval=1, maxval=50, group="Entry", tooltip="Already on a plateau - anything from 5 to 15 works and expectancy degrades above 20. Left unchanged from v2.")
useRisingSlow = input.bool(false, "Require the 200MA to be rising", group="Entry quality (unproven - default off)", tooltip="Did not survive a paired same-date test. Price above a flat or rolling-over 200-day is a trend that has already stopped working. Alone: $75,150 vs $70,029 unfiltered, and drawdown 16.7% vs 21.5%.")
slopeLookback = input.int(20, "200MA slope lookback (bars)", minval=5, group="Entry quality")
useNotExtended = input.bool(false, "Reject entries far above the 50MA", group="Entry quality", tooltip="An RSI(2) dip in a vertical move is a pause, not a pullback to value. Alone: $77,048 and the highest single-filter t of the three.")
maxExtPercent = input.float(8.0, "Max % above the 50MA", minval=1.0, step=0.5, group="Entry quality")
useRelStrength = input.bool(false, "Require outperformance vs benchmark", group="Entry quality", tooltip="Buy dips in leaders; a dip in a laggard is just a laggard. The strongest single filter: $90,895 alone against $70,029 unfiltered.")
benchSymbol = input.symbol("AMEX:SPY", "Benchmark", group="Entry quality")
rsLookback = input.int(60, "Relative strength lookback (bars)", minval=10, group="Entry quality")
useVolRegime = input.bool(false, "Require calm ATR regime", group="Entry", tooltip="Design-set evidence only; not holdout-validated. Off by default.")
atrRankLength = input.int(252, "ATR percentile lookback", minval=50, group="Entry")
atrRankMax = input.float(60.0, "Max ATR percentile", minval=5.0, maxval=100.0, step=5.0, group="Entry")

useFixedDollar = input.bool(true, "Size by fixed dollars per trade", group="Sizing", tooltip="On (default): equal dollars per position, which is what the pooled and portfolio statistics measure. Off: size so the initial stop costs riskPercent of equity, which equalises dollar risk but makes notional vary inversely with ATR.")
dollarsPerTrade = input.float(2500.0, "Dollars per trade", minval=50.0, step=50.0, group="Sizing", tooltip="Set this to equity divided by the number of concurrent positions you intend to run. $2,500 is 1/20th of a $50,000 account, the configuration the portfolio results were measured on.")
riskPercent = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval=0.05, maxval=25.0, step=0.05, group="Sizing", tooltip="Only used when fixed-dollar sizing is off. 1% of $50,000 = $500 lost if the 4.5-ATR stop is hit. Do NOT size so a single loss is a large fraction of the account: the win rate here is ~52%, so losing streaks are longer than v2's.")

tradeMode = input.string("Conservative", "Mode", options=["Conservative", "Aggressive", "Custom"], group="Mode", tooltip="Conservative = the v2 settings: 70% scale-out, 3 ATR stop, breakeven after scaling, 15/40 bar caps. Aggressive = no scale-out, 12 ATR stop, no breakeven, 250 bar cap - one win in three, wins roughly ten times larger. Custom uses the Exits inputs below verbatim.")

atrLength = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval=2, group="Exits")
stopAtrMultInput = input.float(3.0, "Initial stop (ATR multiple)", minval=0.5, step=0.5, group="Exits", tooltip="Left at v2's 3.0. Widening to 4.5 raises full-sample return but deepens per-trade losses in every bear market tested, which is the trade v4 is deliberately not making.")
scalePercentInput = input.int(70, "Sell this % at snapback", minval=0, maxval=100, group="Exits", tooltip="Left at 70. Lowering it to 30 raises full-sample return substantially, but the large scale-out is doing genuine defensive work: it is why bear-market trades lose less here than under v3. Lower it only if you intend to hold through busts.")
snapbackLength = input.int(10, "Snapback MA length", minval=2, group="Exits")
trailAtrMultInput = input.float(3.0, "Chandelier trail (ATR multiple)", minval=0.5, step=0.5, group="Exits", tooltip="Left at v2's 3.0. The 3.0-6.0 plateau favours the wider end on full-sample return, at the cost of deeper bear-market losses.")
useBreakevenStopInput = input.bool(true, "Move stop to breakeven after scaling", group="Exits", tooltip="Kept on. It costs some expectancy over the full history and buys roughly 7pp of win rate; v2's claim of no detectable cost does not hold on this sample.")
maxHoldBeforeScaleInput = input.int(15, "Max bars before scaling", minval=1, group="Exits", tooltip="On a plateau - 15 and 25 are indistinguishable, 8 and below hurt. Unchanged.")
maxHoldRunnerInput = input.int(40, "Max bars for runner", minval=1, group="Exits")

// Mode presets override the Exits inputs unless Custom is selected.
isCons = tradeMode == "Conservative"
isAggr = tradeMode == "Aggressive"
stopAtrMult = isCons ? 3.0 : isAggr ? 12.0 : stopAtrMultInput
scalePercent = isCons ? 70 : isAggr ? 0 : scalePercentInput
trailAtrMult = isCons ? 3.0 : isAggr ? 12.0 : trailAtrMultInput
useBreakevenStop = isCons ? true : isAggr ? false : useBreakevenStopInput
maxHoldBeforeScale = isCons ? 15 : isAggr ? 250 : maxHoldBeforeScaleInput
maxHoldRunner = isCons ? 40 : isAggr ? 250 : maxHoldRunnerInput

fastMA = ta.sma(close, fastLength)
slowMA = ta.sma(close, slowLength)
snapbackMA = ta.sma(close, snapbackLength)
pullbackRSI = ta.rsi(close, rsiLength)
atrValue = ta.atr(atrLength)
atrRank = ta.percentrank(atrValue, atrRankLength)

slowRising = slowMA > slowMA[slopeLookback]
extended = close > fastMA * (1.0 + maxExtPercent / 100.0)
benchClose = request.security(benchSymbol, timeframe.period, close)
// guard the divisions: a young chart or a bad benchmark symbol leaves these na,
// and na comparisons are false, which would silently block every entry
stockRet = close[rsLookback] > 0 ? close / close[rsLookback] : na
benchRet = benchClose[rsLookback] > 0 ? benchClose / benchClose[rsLookback] : na
relStrength = na(stockRet) or na(benchRet) ? na : stockRet / benchRet
rsOk = not useRelStrength or (not na(relStrength) and relStrength > 1.0)
risingOk = not useRisingSlow or slowRising
extOk = not useNotExtended or not extended
entryQuality = risingOk and extOk and rsOk

uptrend = fastMA > slowMA and close > slowMA
regimeOk = useVolRegime ? atrRank <= atrRankMax : true
buySignal = uptrend and regimeOk and entryQuality and pullbackRSI < rsiThreshold

stopDistance = stopAtrMult * atrValue
riskCapital = strategy.equity * riskPercent / 100.0
riskPerUnit = stopDistance * syminfo.pointvalue
rawQty = riskPerUnit > 0 ? riskCapital / riskPerUnit : 0.0
affordableQty = close > 0 ? strategy.equity / close : 0.0
fixedQty = close > 0 ? dollarsPerTrade / close : 0.0
targetQty = useFixedDollar ? fixedQty : rawQty
plannedQty = math.floor(math.min(targetQty, affordableQty))
plannedRisk = plannedQty * stopDistance * syminfo.pointvalue
// math.floor() silently skips the entry when the target is under one share, and it
// skips the HIGHEST-ATR names first, which quietly removes exactly the symbols this
// configuration gains most from. Plotted so it is visible rather than invisible.
sizeSkipped = buySignal and strategy.position_size <= 0 and plannedQty < 1

var float entryStopDistance = na
var float peakHigh = na
var bool hasScaled = false

if buySignal and strategy.position_size <= 0 and plannedQty >= 1
    strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty=plannedQty)
    entryStopDistance := stopDistance
    peakHigh := high
    hasScaled := false

// State is derived from strategy.opentrades rather than tracked by hand: with
// process_orders_on_close the entry fills after this bar's script run, so any
// "reset when flat" block would wipe entry state on the entry bar itself and
// silently disable every exit for the life of the trade.
inPosition = strategy.opentrades > 0
entryIndex = inPosition ? strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(0) : na
if inPosition
    peakHigh := math.max(nz(peakHigh, high), high)

baseStopLevel = na(entryStopDistance) ? na : strategy.position_avg_price - entryStopDistance
// Once the scale-out is booked the runner should not be allowed to drag the blended
// trade negative, so the stop ratchets up to the entry price. Note this is breakeven
// on PRICE, not after costs: commission and slippage make it a small net loss.
stopLevel = hasScaled and useBreakevenStop and not na(baseStopLevel) ? math.max(baseStopLevel, strategy.position_avg_price) : baseStopLevel
chandelierLevel = na(peakHigh) ? na : peakHigh - trailAtrMult * atrValue
heldBars = na(entryIndex) ? 0 : bar_index - entryIndex
canManage = inPosition and heldBars > 0

if inPosition and not na(stopLevel)
    strategy.exit("Hard stop", "Long", stop=stopLevel)

scaleSignal = canManage and not hasScaled and scalePercent > 0 and close > snapbackMA
if scaleSignal
    strategy.close("Long", qty_percent=scalePercent, comment="Scale at snapback")
    hasScaled := true

trailSignal = canManage and hasScaled and not na(chandelierLevel) and close < chandelierLevel
trendSignal = canManage and close < slowMA
timeSignal = canManage and (hasScaled ? heldBars >= maxHoldRunner : heldBars >= maxHoldBeforeScale)
exitSignal = trailSignal or trendSignal or timeSignal
if exitSignal
    exitReason = trailSignal ? "Chandelier trail" : trendSignal ? "Trend break" : "Max hold"
    strategy.close("Long", comment=exitReason)

// The hard stop fills broker-side through strategy.exit, so it never raises exitSignal
// and a stopped-out trade would leave no mark on the chart. Detect the touch directly.
stopHit = canManage and not na(stopLevel) and low <= stopLevel

plot(fastMA, "50-day MA", color=color.new(color.blue, 0), linewidth=2)
plot(slowMA, "200-day MA", color=color.new(color.orange, 0), linewidth=2)
plot(snapbackMA, "Snapback MA", color=color.new(color.gray, 45), linewidth=1)
plot(inPosition ? stopLevel : na, "Hard stop", color=color.new(color.red, 20), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(inPosition and hasScaled ? chandelierLevel : na, "Chandelier trail", color=color.new(color.purple, 10), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plotshape(uptrend and regimeOk and pullbackRSI < rsiThreshold and not entryQuality and strategy.position_size <= 0, title="Filtered out", text="SKIP", style=shape.labelup, location=location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.gray, 40), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
bgcolor(uptrend ? color.new(color.green, 92) : color.new(color.red, 94), title="Trend regime")
plotshape(buySignal and strategy.position_size <= 0 and plannedQty >= 1, title="BUY", text="BUY", style=shape.labelup, location=location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.green, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plotshape(sizeSkipped, title="SKIPPED (size < 1 share)", text="SIZE", style=shape.labelup, location=location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.gray, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(scaleSignal, title="SELL PARTIAL", text="SELL PT", style=shape.labeldown, location=location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.blue, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(exitSignal and not stopHit, title="SELL ALL", text="SELL", style=shape.labeldown, location=location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plotshape(stopHit, title="SELL ON STOP", text="SELL", style=shape.labeldown, location=location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.maroon, 0), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)

if buySignal and strategy.position_size <= 0 and plannedQty >= 1
    alert("BUY: RSI(2) pullback inside 50/200 uptrend. Stop " + str.tostring(stopAtrMult) + " ATR.", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if sizeSkipped
    alert("SKIPPED: signal fired but the position rounds to under one share. Raise capital or dollarsPerTrade.", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if scaleSignal
    alert("SELL PART: selling " + str.tostring(scalePercent) + "% into the snapback above the short MA; trailing the remainder.", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if exitSignal and not stopHit
    alert("SELL ALL: chandelier trail, trend break, or max hold reached.", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if stopHit
    alert("SELL ALL (stop): hard stop touched at " + str.tostring(math.round_to_mintick(stopLevel)) + ".", alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

alertcondition(buySignal and strategy.position_size <= 0, "TDPS v3 BUY", "Pullback entry inside uptrend")
alertcondition(exitSignal or stopHit, "TDPS v3 SELL", "Exit signal")
